Use Case :  Reivew the PR and get it approved or Rejected in Azure Repos

What Agent will do on a high Level 

Listens for (or is triggered on) a PR in Azure Repos.

Pulls the diff + changed files and PR metadata.

Uses LLM-only to produce a baseline review.

Uses RAG (your org’s guidelines) via LangChain + FAISS to produce a policy-aligned review with inline suggestions and patch snippets.

Posts a review comment to the PR and (optionally) sets Approve / Wait for author / Reject by voting via the Azure DevOps API.

Runs safely in dry-run by default (so nothing is posted until you’re ready).


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


| Layer          | Tool                                  | Why it’s needed                                                         |                                            |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Compute        | **AWS EC2 (Linux)**                   | Where the agent runs (cron/manual/webhook worker).                      |                                            |
| Language Model | **Mistral (mistralai)** or **OpenAI** | Core reasoning: detect issues, propose fixes, generate patch snippets.  |                                            |
| Orchestration  | **LangChain**                         | Chains + prompt templates + integrates vector search.                   |                                            |
| Retrieval      | **RAG (FAISS + embeddings)**          | Grounds the review with your org’s **style/security/performance** docs. |                                            |
| Embeddings     | **sentence-transformers**             | Turns your `.txt/.md` guidelines into vectors for semantic search.      |                                            |
| Vector DB      | **FAISS (CPU)**                       | Fast, local vector search on EC2.                                       |                                            |
| VCS API        | **Azure DevOps REST API**             | Read PRs, diffs, create review comments, set vote (Approve/Reject).     |                                            |
| Python         | `requests`, `dataclasses`             | Glue, API calls, IO, CLI.                                               |                                            |
| Secrets        | Env variables                         | `AZDO_PAT`, `AZDO_ORG_URL`, `AZDO_PROJECT`, `AZDO_REPO_ID               | |

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Prerequisites :

Azure DevOps Personal Access Token (PAT)

Scopes: Code (Read & Write).

Export: export AZDO_PAT="..."

Azure DevOps info

AZDO_ORG_URL (e.g., https://dev.azure.com/<org>)

AZDO_PROJECT

AZDO_REPO_ID or AZDO_REPO_NAME

The PR number you want to review.

LLM key

Mistral: export MISTRAL_API_KEY="..." (or use OpenAI if you prefer).

RAG docs (put in docs/ on EC2)

style_guide.txt, security_checklist.txt, performance_guidelines.txt

Add any org-specific policies you want the agent to site

